# MadGraph5 batch script: p p > b b~ QCD=2 at a fixed scale.
#
# Why this exact process:
#   - The only multi-channel row whose hard process carries no electroweak core.
#     The Drell-Yan groups (pp_to_ll, pp_to_llj_fixed) are held together by an
#     s-channel gamma*/Z and every member shares one colour structure, so their
#     flavour union varies the electroweak couplings and little else. A b b~ pair
#     at QCD order 2 spans two initial states whose colour content differs — g g
#     resolved through the triple-gluon vertex, and q q~ through a single
#     s-channel gluon — so the group's members differ in the part of the
#     amplitude the colour code owns.
#   - It is the first cross section and event sample gated on the mirrored beam
#     ordering. g g is symmetric under exchanging the beams; q q~ is not, and the
#     q u~ ordering the enumeration does not produce is what the mirror term
#     supplies. In the Drell-Yan groups that path carries a cross section too,
#     but no row was gated on a group where the mirrored members are this large a
#     share.
#
# Same generate line as pp_to_bb_qcd2. The run card differs in three places,
# each for the reason pp_to_llj_fixed's does:
#
#   - fixed_ren_scale / fixed_fac_scale1 / fixed_fac_scale2 = True, all three
#     scales at m_Z. The dynamical default (dynamical_scale_choice = -1) needs
#     the general kT clustering, which coupling::scales refuses rather than
#     approximates; a constant scale takes the branch that has a closed form, so
#     this run's per-event SCALUP / <rscale> / <pdfrwt> can be replayed exactly.
#     This is what pp_to_bb and pp_to_bb_qcd2 cannot offer and why neither has an
#     integrals or samples cell.
#   - pdlabel = lhapdf with lhaid 247000 (NNPDF23_lo_as_0130_qed). The
#     MG-internal nn23lo1 that pp_to_bb takes is not an LHAPDF6 grid and cannot
#     be read by this crate's PDF layer; 247000 is the set the Drell-Yan and llj
#     references already use.
#   - ptb 20 and etab 5, where pp_to_bb leaves both open. Uncut, the cross
#     section is 4.2e8 pb and is dominated by the region where the 4.7 GeV b mass
#     is the only regulator, so a comparison there would measure the collinear
#     limit rather than the colour and flavour content this row exists for. It is
#     the analogue of pp_to_llj_fixed's mmll = 50, and it leaves the uncut region
#     covered by nothing — deliberately, since no cross section on this side
#     reproduces it without a scale prescription anyway.
#
# Everything else is left where pp_to_bb had it.
generate p p > b b~ QCD=2
output pp_to_bb_fixed -nojpeg
launch
  set ebeam1 6500
  set ebeam2 6500
  set fixed_ren_scale True
  set fixed_fac_scale1 True
  set fixed_fac_scale2 True
  set scale 91.188
  set dsqrt_q2fact1 91.188
  set dsqrt_q2fact2 91.188
  set pdlabel lhapdf
  set lhaid 247000
  set ptb 20
  set etab 5
  done
